      "reason": "Index33 correction 2: added a bounded server-side drain step (drain_in_flight_requests()/TrafficOrchestrator.drain_server_side_requests()), called from TrafficSyncedWrapper.step() immediately after stop_episode_traffic() at every episode boundary. Index32 diagnosis: stop_generator() only terminates the CLIENT-side generator process; server-side in-flight /work requests were never drained or awaited before the next episode's reset() began consuming its own separate 120s restoration_max_wait_s budget, letting stale CPU-starvation/probe-failure effects from the ending episode bleed into and consume the next episode's reset window. The new step polls the EXISTING demo_app_requests_in_progress Prometheus gauge (no new metric), bounded by a new, much-smaller DEFAULT_DRAIN_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=30s/DEFAULT_DRAIN_POLL_INTERVAL_SECONDS=2s, raising a new DrainTimeoutError/DrainQueryError (never silently continuing) on failure. No traffic profile, intensity, DEFAULT_MAX_IN_FLIGHT, seed, schedule identity, probe threshold/timing, CPU/memory resource, or restoration_max_wait_s change."
    },
